# COPIED-METHOD-DECLARED-FORMAL and COPIED-CALLABLE-ACTUAL, the route by callable reference: run's formal g receives
# b1\getq -- the copy's own occurrence of getq, the one the path selects -- and the unit's getq: one method, one
# native code, one class, two occurrences with different parents.  g(w) admits w in the space of the occurrence g
# holds; getq reads its node's tag: the copy's 1 (copied at the merge), the unit's 5 (written after).  HEAD handed
# the unit's occurrence for the path (45, 45).  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 2
end: Wide
int: tag 1
fn: getq (Wide: q) int
    return: q\x * 10 + node\tag
end: getq
Box:
    int: v 0
    fn: getq
end: Box
fn: run (getq: g; Wide: w) int
    return: g(w)
end: run
b1: merge: Box
w: merge: Wide
w\x: 4
tag: 5
int: r run(b1\getq; w)
int: s run(getq; w)
int: ok 7
if: r != 41 || s != 45
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
